--- R0
+++ R1
@@ -49,2 +49,20 @@
   _hook_: '*'
+# Break ACTION-level loops: the model issues the exact same Bash command
+# many times in a row (18-29 verbatim repeats observed on the R0
+# budget_exceeded cluster). Strategy 1 (exact name+inputs) injects an
+# escalating "you are looping — try something fundamentally different"
+# warning into each repeated tool result from repeat 3 onward, then
+# raises LoopDetectedError at repeat 8 to reclaim budget on hopeless
+# verbatim loops. Warn-before-raise gives the model several chances to
+# self-correct and finish before the run is terminated. Strategy 2
+# (name-only) is warn-only and, because the only tool is Bash, is
+# effectively disabled by a high name_warn_threshold so it does not
+# false-positive on legitimate multi-command work.
+- _target_: harnessx.processors.control.loop_detection.LoopDetectionProcessor
+  window_size: 12
+  warn_threshold: 3
+  threshold: 8
+  name_warn_threshold: 999
+  compaction_drop_threshold: 5
+  _hook_: '*'
 - _target_: harnessx.processors.control.compaction.CompactionProcessor